    "adapt": "A hostless plot above a sea cove: no building, so the kit never turns. Every row rests on the probed ground (`--terrain`) inside the plot's 2 m margin. The fishing spot stands on the plot's north edge, 14 m north of its centre; the cove's water lies 16 to 21 m further north, inside the spot's 30 m radius, so a cast from the beach lands in it. The bench and lantern stand beside the spot, the bench facing the water, and the sign stands back on the grass facing the land. Rows are rigid: shift, never stretch."
